        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(commands): bound reset-hook transcript reads to prevent OOM",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`loadBeforeResetTranscript` in `src/auto-reply/reply/commands-reset-hooks.ts` reads session transcript JSONL files with unbounded `fs.promises.readFile` calls. A runaway or corrupted transcript file could force the `before_reset` hook path to buffer the entire file into memory, leading to OOM.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe sibling gateway reset path already uses `readSessionMessagesAsync`, the streaming session transcript reader, to build `before_reset` hook payloads without whole-file buffering. Routing the command reset path through the same reader seam:\n\n- Avoids buffering arbitrarily large transcripts into memory.\n- Preserves messages for large-but-valid transcripts instead of dropping them.\n- Reuses the existing reset-archive fallback and leaf-control behavior.\n\n## User Impact\n\n`before_reset` hooks no longer risk process OOM from oversized transcripts, and they continue to receive the transcript messages for legitimate large sessions.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Replaced the uncapped `fs.readFile` path and the 16 MiB hard cap with `readSessionMessagesAsync({ mode: \"full\", allowResetArchiveFallback: true })` in `src/auto-reply/reply/commands-reset-hooks.ts`.\n- Updated `src/auto-reply/reply/commands-core.test.ts` to mock the transcript reader and verify the command path passes the correct scope and reset-archive fallback option.\n- Removed the obsolete oversized-file cap test from `src/auto-reply/reply/commands-reset-hooks.test.ts`.\n- Local focused runs pass:\n  - `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/auto-reply/reply/commands-core.test.ts --run`\n  - `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/auto-reply/reply/commands-reset-hooks.test.ts --run`\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\nI ran a standalone Node script that patches the global hook runner, calls `emitResetCommandHooks` from `src/auto-reply/reply/commands-reset-hooks.ts` with a `previousSessionEntry.sessionFile` containing ~83,887 valid message lines (~16 MiB total), and records the `before_reset` hook payload:\n\n```text\n$ node --import tsx /tmp/proof-101479-reader.mjs\nDirect reader returned 83887 messages\nPR #101479 real behavior proof: reset-hook command path via transcript reader\nTranscript size: 16304909 bytes (>16777216 bytes)\nMessage lines written: 83887\nbefore_reset hook fired: true\nHook event messages count: 83887\nPASS: oversized valid transcript preserved hook messages via streaming reader\n```\n\nThe actual `emitResetCommandHooks` path invoked `runBeforeReset` with all 83,887 messages, confirming that the streaming reader prevents whole-file buffering without dropping large valid transcripts.",
        "branch": "fix/bound-reset-hook-transcript-read",
